WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.275
What does it leave to you?

2
00:00:01.275 --> 00:00:02.917
The requests create one app,

3
00:00:02.917 --> 00:00:07.701
but nothing reads all of them back with
their segments and assignments, so the kit

4
00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:12.200
has a read for that, marked unverified,
and the lab compares it with the portal.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.587
A group with one inactive
connector looks fine in a list,

6
00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:17.575
so the kit counts active members.

7
00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:23.625
A wide range on every port is the VPN
again, so wide segments and overlaps fail.

8
00:00:23.625 --> 00:00:27.138
A person assigned directly
escapes the access review.

9
00:00:27.138 --> 00:00:32.745
Plain MFA on RDP passes a casual
look, so any app covering port 22

10
00:00:32.745 --> 00:00:39.000
or 3389 needs the phishing-resistant
strength and a compliant device.

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.570
And Quick Access is
tracked until it's empty.
